@startuml
title ShardPilot: explicit selection and independent outcome gates
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam activityBorderColor #2563EB
skinparam ArrowColor #475569

start
:Consumer supplies immutable YAML v1 manifest;
:Adapter discovers full eligible classes E;
if (Nonempty, unique and requested subset of E?) then (yes)
  :Expand selected families within E only;
  :Retain E and selected baseline S separately;
  :Write suite / manifest hash / expansion report;
  :Restrict timing history to selected families;
  :Plan S for count >= 1;
  fork
    :Write selected baseline and planned-N.yaml;
    :Record common selection identity;
  fork again
    :Apply subset and shard filter;
    :Check native candidate equality before NO-SOURCE;
    :Write actual-N.yaml and identity sidecar;
    :Native runner executes tests;
    :Native test-result / CI job gate;
  end fork
  :Read original collected evidence;
  :Verify identity, partition and per-node selections;
  :Write separate coverage JSON and HTML;
  :Require coverage AND native outcome gates;
else (no)
  :Fail before native execution;
  :Never fall back to the full suite;
endif
stop
@enduml
